# UNTESTED_ON_LG200

**No LG200 hardware execution has been performed. The user explicitly waived the LG200 validation gate for this experimental build; no hardware decoding, picture correctness, performance, or stability claim is made.**

This package contains the source-built LoongVPU VA-API driver at fixed upstream commit 8d95205627f83f6b36d09a9263ac9f381959c6c3, with only the reviewed capability-truthfulness patch applied.

It is an explicit opt-in experiment, not a silent upgrade of the vendor loongvpu package. It Provides, Conflicts with, and Replaces loongvpu so that installing loongvpu-open is a deliberate package-manager transaction.

The files loongvpu_drv_video.so and loonggpu_drv_video.so select the same open driver. The second name is a relative symbolic link for libva compatibility. No other vendor driver name is claimed.

## No LS9A support or all-platform equivalence

The vendor loongvpu package also installs ls9a_3b6600_vpu.so. Explicitly replacing that package can therefore remove this vendor file; this experiment does not provide an ls9a_3b6600_vpu.so symlink or equivalent implementation. Default driver selection and functionality on 3B6000M/LS9A are unverified. Any future release gate must test that machine class or explicitly restrict the supported scope.

## Runtime and vendor prerm risk

Runtime dependencies preserve the vendor package's minimum LoongGPU driver, LoongVPU kernel DKMS, and libva requirements. The open userspace driver still requires the corresponding kernel and GPU stack; a successful isolated libva load does not remove those prerequisites.

The official loongvpu prerm removes `/usr/share/glvnd/egl_vendor.d/40_loonggpu.json`. A package transaction that replaces or removes the vendor package can run that script and delete this EGL vendor JSON on a target system. This experiment neither owns nor restores that file. It is absent and not dpkg-owned on the packaging LG110, but target systems must back it up and verify/restage it during rollback as applicable.

## Source, copyright and rebuild

The exact patched upstream source, complete REL6 recipe, license notices, and rebuild instructions are embedded at `/usr/share/doc/loongvpu-open/source.tar.xz`. See `REBUILD.md`, `copyright`, `SOURCE-AND-LICENSE`, `LICENSE-PACKAGING`, and `licenses/` in the same documentation directory.

The fixed upstream commit declares MIT but has no standalone LICENSE file. The included MIT full text is explicitly a downstream standard-text copy based on that declaration. VC8000D BSD-3-Clause and kernel GPL-2.0-only notices are reproduced from the pinned corresponding sources; no third-party code is relicensed as original packaging work.

## Validation boundary

Validation on the packaging LG110 host is limited to compilation, unit and capability tests, package inspection, isolated libva loading, and source-archive rebuild comparison. This host has no LoongVPU render node. Soft-degrade vainfo is not hardware decode evidence.

Do not install this package for ordinary production use. Independent verifier PASS is required before any deploy. See the accompanying external REPORT.md and ROLLBACK.md for exact evidence and reversal steps.
